              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Experimentation with Style</strong><br>\nThroughout his career, Pissarro experimented with different styles and techniques. He worked closely with Georges Seurat and Paul Signac, adopting their pointillist approach for a period before returning to his distinct Impressionist style.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Political Involvement</strong><br>\nPissarro's work was influenced by his socio-political views. As an anarchist, he believed in egalitarian principles, which were reflected in his dignified depictions of laborers and his emphasis on rural and urban community life.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Challenges and Persistence</strong><br>\nPissarro's work was often met with criticism, and he struggled financially for most of his life. Despite these challenges, he continued to paint, firmly adhering to his artistic convictions and the pursuit of his vision.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
